<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Roomy is intentionally NOT sandboxed: reading Photos/Mail/Messages/other
	apps' data and Time Machine local snapshots requires Full Disk Access,
	which is incompatible with the App Sandbox. This file deliberately
	contains no com.apple.security.app-sandbox key.

	Hardened Runtime (required for notarization, Release builds only — see
	Project.swift) is otherwise maximally restrictive by default: no JIT, no
	unsigned executable memory, no disabled library validation, none of
	which Roomy needs. The one exception below is real:
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
	<!--
	CategoryCoordinator.emptyTrash() sends Finder an Apple Event ("empty
	trash") rather than deleting ~/.Trash's contents directly, since Finder
	owns Trash semantics that a raw filesystem delete would bypass. Sending
	Apple Events to another app is one of the few things Hardened Runtime
	blocks by default even for a non-sandboxed app, and macOS still prompts
	the user for this via TCC's Automation permission (NSAppleEventsUsageDescription
	in Info.plist is the prompt's explanation text) independent of Hardened
	Runtime — this entitlement only makes the capability possible at all.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
